    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d457">

                <pb facs="0548" n="468" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg468"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Choate</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-11-21"><hi rendition="#italic">November 21,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 500.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose a copy of a letter from the Hon.
                    Thomas Hedge, a member of Congress from Iowa, with inclosure, from which it
                    appears that Edward C. Janse, a native of Iowa, who was engaged in railroad
                    building in South Africa, was captured by a British force at Machadodorp while
                    engaged in his work, and was taken to Pretoria, where he is now held as a
                    prisoner of war.</p>
                <p>You will ask for an investigation of the matter and suggest that Mr. Janse be
                    released, if the facts warrant it at this time.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d457-a1.xml" xpointer="d457-a1"/>
